  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14190611/assets/881ec029bea9d85b0f1f76c3c62ca0343b9b6103c57122f6dc06d02cf5b30d8c.png)\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is defined and differentiable on the interval $[-4,4].$ The graph of $y={f}^{′}(x),$ the derivative of $f(x),$ is given above, where the areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $8,5$ and $6,$ respectively (from left to right). Find $f(4)$ if $f(-4)=-1.$",
